---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
/**
 * Incorporated by reference into /terms. This is the document that makes
 * upstream platform obligations flow downstream to customers — if a seller
 * breaches a messaging platform's policy through our product, the platform
 * comes after us.
 */
---

<Legal
  title="Acceptable Use Policy"
  description="What you may and may not do with iGrowFast — particularly around messaging people."
  path="/acceptable-use"
  updated="16 July 2026"
  summary="What you may and may not do with iGrowFast. Most of it is obvious; the messaging rules are the ones that catch people out."
>
  <h2 id="scope">Scope</h2>
  <p>
    This policy is part of the <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>. It applies
    to you and to everyone you give an account to. If any of it is breached, we
    can suspend or terminate — and we will tell you why.
  </p>

  <h2 id="messaging">Messaging — read this part properly</h2>
  <p>
    This is where real damage happens, to your customers and to your own
    accounts. Messaging platforms enforce these rules aggressively and they
    enforce them against the number sending the message, which is yours.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Do not message people who did not ask to hear from you.</strong>
      You need a lawful basis and, for marketing, you need consent. Buying a
      phone list is not consent. Scraping numbers is not consent.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Consent is per purpose.</strong> Someone agreeing to delivery
      updates has not agreed to promotions.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Honour opt-outs immediately.</strong> If someone says stop, stop — across every number you operate.</li>
    <li><strong>Keep the record.</strong> If you cannot show when and how someone opted in, you do not have consent.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Do not use the service to evade a platform's limits</strong> — no
      rotating numbers to dodge a block, no artificial spreading of a blast to
      look organic, no circumventing a rate limit or a ban.
    </li>
    <li>Do not impersonate anyone, including us or a courier or a platform.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The messaging platform's own policies apply on top of this and win where
    they are stricter. Breaching them can get your number banned permanently, and
    we cannot get it back for you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="prohibited">Prohibited content and industries</h2>
  <p>
    You may not use iGrowFast to sell, promote or facilitate:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Anything illegal where it is being sold or delivered.</li>
    <li>Drugs, controlled substances, tobacco, vaping or alcohol where prohibited.</li>
    <li>Weapons, ammunition, explosives.</li>
    <li>Prescription medicines, medical devices, or supplements making medical claims.</li>
    <li>Counterfeit or infringing goods.</li>
    <li>Live animals, human body parts, endangered species products.</li>
    <li>Adult content or services.</li>
    <li>Gambling, lotteries, betting.</li>
    <li>Financial products, lending, cryptocurrency, or investment offers.</li>
    <li>Multi-level marketing, pyramid schemes, "get rich quick" offers.</li>
    <li>Stolen goods, hacking tools, fraudulent documents.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some of these are lawful somewhere and still prohibited here, because the
    platforms we connect to prohibit them. That is not us being cautious for its
    own sake — it is the condition of the integrations working at all.
  </p>

  <h2 id="deceptive">No deception</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No misrepresenting what you sell, what it costs, or when it arrives.</li>
    <li>No fake reviews, fake testimonials, or fabricated urgency.</li>
    <li>No dark patterns designed to make someone accept a delivery they did not agree to.</li>
    <li>No baiting an order with one product and delivering another.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="technical">Technical</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No scraping, crawling, or bulk-extracting from the service beyond your own data via features we provide.</li>
    <li>No probing, scanning, or attempting to breach the service or another tenant's data. If you find a vulnerability, tell us — we will not come after you for reporting it in good faith.</li>
    <li>No overloading the service or interfering with anyone else's use of it.</li>
    <li>No reselling, sublicensing, or white-labelling without our written agreement.</li>
    <li>No uploading malware.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="data">Other people's data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Only upload data you are entitled to hold.</li>
    <li>Do not upload special-category data — health, religion, politics, biometrics, sexual orientation — into fields not designed for it. Our product is not built to protect it and you probably have no basis to hold it.</li>
    <li>Do not use another business's customer data because it happened to pass through a shared number.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="ai">AI features</h2>
  <p>
    <span class="wip">Not yet in production</span> Where AI-assisted features
    exist in future, you may not use them to generate deceptive content, to
    impersonate a person, or to make automated decisions about people that have
    legal or similarly significant effects. Where a message is machine-generated
    and a person could reasonably think otherwise, that must be disclosed.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sanctions">Sanctions</h2>
  <p>
    You may not use the service in breach of US sanctions law. See
    <a href="/terms#sanctions">Terms, section 7</a> for the current scope.
  </p>

  <h2 id="enforce">How we enforce</h2>
  <p>
    Proportionately. Usually we ask you to fix it. For serious or urgent harm —
    ongoing unlawful activity, a live security threat, a platform demanding
    action — we may suspend first and explain immediately after. We would rather
    talk to you than terminate you.
  </p>
  <p>
    To report abuse of this policy by another user: <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
